"The taxi reached in front of my building," I told Sara and Kiran.
"I had one big bag with me."
"My room was on the top floor."
"So I took the bag and climbed the stairs."
"Did you carry that bag alone?"
Kiran asked suddenly.
"Yes, the bag was very heavy," I replied.
"I walked up very slowly."
"Finally, I reached in front of my room's door."
"That evening, I stepped out of the room."
"Near the stairs, I met my neighbor, Anitha."
"She looked at me and smiled happily."
"On the first day itself, she helped me a lot."
Hearing this, Sara laughed.
"Getting a good neighbor on the very first day is great luck," Sara said.
I agreed to that completely.
"Yes, I felt a great relief that day," I said.
